			<div class="content" id="post-content-2036036">
									

<p>You had <em>one job</em>, butterfly.</p>
<p>This is what would’ve been my SCP-2000 contest entry, had I gotten past the brainstorming/scrawl notes in my notebook stage.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Show&nbsp;spoilers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">hide&nbsp;spoilers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Basically, the Foundation in some other time/space/whatever managed to manufacture a means to send messages between parallel dimensions. The messengers are these butterflies made of light and human brain cells, who have enough embedded intelligence to communicate as well as relay the messages they were created to store.</p>
<p>Mark Kiryu in one dimension (where these butterfly messengers are commonplace) was trying to send a message to Mark Kiryu in another dimension but some funky space stuff happened and another butterfly smacked into it. Basically, two of them en route to the same message delivery spot got mushed up by accident and ended up in the wrong time/space/dimension. The resulting butterfly is basically waiting for the parallel universe it came from to right itself so it can go home.</p>
<p>Different kinds of light are like food to these butterflies. You are what you eat. d: This one happens to like ultraviolet light while blue light makes it feel nauseous.<br /></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Many thanks to all these nice people who read this over in chat! /deep breath ProcyonLotor, Riemann, Gaffsey, MisterFlames, Zolgamax, Eskobear, Devereaux, Gamerkid2345, TheTyrantis, TroyL, TwistedGears, Athena_Grey, Kalinin, Ihp(kmn) Sorry if I forgot anyone.</p>
<p>Some easy easter eggs, look up the NGC 6302 nebula and the etymology of the word “angel”. ;)</p>
<hr />
