			<div class="content" id="post-content-2036447">
									

<p>As stated previously in chat, I'm close to an upvote on this one. I enjoyed the interview, which is a neat trick because interviews are difficult to write successfully, both from the proper execution and article enhancement angles. As a whole, there's a pleasant degree of puzzlement that I get from this article; not enough is given away to make things immediately apparent, but it's not so veiled as to be meaningless nonsense.</p>
<p>That said, I'm left with the feeling that I've read three-quarters of a good novel, and it's stopped before I've found anything out. That's okay sometimes, since mystery is a frequently employed tool around here that I enjoy very much, but this needs just a little bit more to get it over the finish line. Not much more, because I don't want this clearly explained and in a sense disenchanted, but maybe just a little more suggestion. I mean, what <em>kind</em> of message is this? Hints of that nature could add an extra layer to this article in terms of the background tone. As it stands, I'm in high neutral-vote territory.</p>

							</div>

								
					
